{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "paper",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 40,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# Commit–Abstain Circuit\n\nNguyen et al. · arXiv:2609.32964v2\n\n[Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.32964v2) · [Code](https://github.com/vnht/commit-abstain-circuit)\n\nRead columns left → right. Cards link to source pages.\n\nResults are author-reported.",
      "section": "Source",
      "status": "source",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=1"
    },
    {
      "id": "question",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 400,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# Why answer anyway?\n\nCan internal uncertainty coexist with confident answers?\n\nAuthors investigate commitment despite insufficient information.\n\n[§1 · p.2](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=2)",
      "section": "Introduction",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=2"
    },
    {
      "id": "scope",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# Scope\n\nUnanswerable questions; instruction-tuned models.\n\nAnswer correctness and later generation dynamics remain outside the main analysis.\n\nLexical abstention tokens and fixed-normalisation attribution approximate behaviour.\n\n[Scope · p.10](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=10)\n\n[Attribution assumption · p.3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=3)",
      "section": "Limitations",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=10"
    },
    {
      "id": "margin",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 490,
      "y": 40,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "# Decision readout\n\n**Δ = max(commit logits) − max(abstain logits)**\n\nΔ ≥ 0: answer; Δ < 0: abstain.\n\n**97.6%** agreement with generated decisions.\n\n[§3 · p.3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=3)",
      "section": "Method",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=3"
    },
    {
      "id": "gates",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 490,
      "y": 400,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "# Find components\n\nFrozen model; train attention/MLP gates with opposing retention/removal pressures.\n\n[Method](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=5)",
      "section": "Method",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=5"
    },
    {
      "id": "sparse",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 490,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "# Sparse circuitry\n\nMedian **5.2%** of components selected.\n\nIncludes attention heads and MLPs.\n\n[§4.4 · p.7](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=7)",
      "section": "Findings",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=7"
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanism",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 40,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "# Earlier commitment\n\nEarly commitment accumulates; later abstention signals often cannot reverse it.\n\n[§4.4 · p.7](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=7)",
      "section": "Findings",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=7"
    },
    {
      "id": "causal",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 400,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "# Causal probes\n\nAblation and amplification support distinct component roles, with error trade-offs.\n\n[§4.5 · p.7](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=7)",
      "section": "Findings",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=7"
    },
    {
      "id": "policy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "# Read components separately\n\nCAC contributions + statistics → small MLP → calibrated abstention.\n\n[§5.1 · p.8](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=8)",
      "section": "Method",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=8"
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluation",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1390,
      "y": 40,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "# Experimental coverage\n\n10 models, 3B–14B.\n\nKUQ · SQuAD 2.0 · MuSiQue.\n\n1,000 examples/dataset; 50/50 split.\n\n[§4.1 · p.4](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=4)",
      "section": "Evaluation",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=4"
    },
    {
      "id": "results",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1390,
      "y": 400,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "# Reported gains\n\nVersus zero-threshold:\n\n- Accuracy: **+12.2 points**\n- False abstention: **0.320 → 0.127**\n\n[Table 2](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=9)",
      "section": "Evaluation",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=9"
    },
    {
      "id": "transfer",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1390,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "# Generalisation\n\nHotpotQA/SelfAware: **+6.9 accuracy points**.\n\n27B/35B extension requires fresh localisation/training.\n\n[§5.2 · p.10](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2#page=10)",
      "section": "Evaluation",
      "status": "reported",
      "path": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.32964v2",
      "anchor": "page=10"
    }
  ],
